    <VASSAL.build.module.StartupGlobalKeyCommand buttonHotkey="" buttonText="" deckCount="0" filter="{CurrentMap==&quot;$cCardPileMap$&quot; &amp;&amp; Type==&quot;CmdDrawCnt&quot;}" hotkey="63743,0,START" icon="" name="Start up message &amp; set global constants (Vassal workaround to allow maintenance of GPs used as constants in pre-set scenarios)" reportFormat="{prefNoWelcome!=true ?Alert(&quot;&lt;html&gt;&lt;p style=width:400px&gt;&lt;color=#003776&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;Commands &amp; Colors: Napoleonics Epic, Version 3.0&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/color&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This module supports automated card management and will configure itself as player slots are taken before a game is started.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Players join the game as normal. Each Corps Commander player must also press the &lt;b&gt;Take Command!&lt;/b&gt; button under the Game Startup menu in that Corp Commander's hand window; this action places a name-tag on screen for the Corps Commander.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;6/8 Player games only: Commander-in-Chief (Allies and French) allocates Tactician Card draws when prompted, by button press or equivalent right-click command.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;To start a game, the French (or Solitaire) player presses the \&quot;Deal Cards\&quot; button (or equivalent right-click command).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Hints &amp; Tips&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;br&gt; &lt;b&gt;Card Play:&lt;/b&gt; Use the right-click commands to play Cards. This avoids potential for cards to be placed into the wrong part of the board which can compromise automated card management for End Turn and Counter-Attack functions.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stacking:&lt;/b&gt; An easy way to access a stacked unit is to select the leader or stack and press left-arrow. To re-stack, press left-arrow again. Some Unit commands automatically re-stack.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;General:&lt;/b&gt; Unit and Leader commands are context sensitive by default. This keeps menus short and reduces errors. This means that, for example, some commands are only available before a unit is Ordered (March Move, Garrison - where valid - and Recover Hit) or when a unit has a combat marker on it (Take Hit and, also, Recover Hit).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This welcome message can be disabled from &lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;Preferences, Game Options...&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;.  Find further assistance via the resources under the &lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;Help&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt; drop-down menu.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/html&gt;&quot;):&quot;&quot; } " reportSingle="true" singleMap="true" tooltip=""/>
